    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nIn this topic, we'll practice evaluating expressions by manipulating and transforming other expressions or equations.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Evaluating an Expression Given X\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: z = 8,] what is the value of [MATH: z + 11?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given that [MATH: z = 8] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: z + 11.]\n\nTo do this, we substitute [MATH: 8] for [MATH: z] in the expression and simplify:\n\n[MATH: z + 11|= 8 + 11; = 19]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: z + 11] is [MATH: 19.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: y = 5,] what is the value of [MATH: y + 18?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 13]\nb. [MATH: 28]\nc. [MATH: 18]\nd. [MATH: 23]\ne. [MATH: 25]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: z = 8,] what is the value of [MATH: z + 11?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 13]\nb. [MATH: 19]\nc. [MATH: 18]\nd. [MATH: 25]\ne. [MATH: 14]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Evaluating an Expression Given kX\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: 7x = 63,] what is the value of [MATH: 7x + 6?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 7x = 63] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: 7x + 6.]\n\nSince we are already told that [MATH: 7x = 63,] we can substitute this value into the expression [MATH: 7x + 6] and simplify:\n\n[MATH: 7x + 6|= 63 + 6; = 69]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: 7x + 6] is [MATH: 69.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 6z = 54,] what is the value of [MATH: 6z + 5?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 64]\nb. [MATH: 60]\nc. [MATH: 49]\nd. [MATH: 54]\ne. [MATH: 59]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 7x = 63,] what is the value of [MATH: 7x + 6?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 69]\nb. [MATH: 66]\nc. [MATH: 70]\nd. [MATH: 63]\ne. [MATH: 75]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Taking an Equation's Reciprocal\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: \\dfrac{a}{2} = 3,] then what is the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{2}{a}?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given that [MATH: \\dfrac{a}{2} = 3] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{2}{a}.]\n\nIt is sufficient to take the reciprocal on both sides of the equation, as follows:\n[MATH: (a)/(2)|= 3; (a)/(2)|= (3)/(1); (2)/(a)|= 1 3]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: (z)/(4) = 7,] then [MATH: (4)/(z) =][FREE_ENTRY 1].\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: (a)/(2) = 3,] then [MATH: (2)/(a) =][FREE_ENTRY 1]."
